# Deterministic checkouts across platforms.
#
# api/public_assets.py embeds the exact bytes of the allowlisted public/ assets
# (base64 + sha256). Those hashes are the tamper-evidence surface for the
# hosted adapter, so the working-tree bytes must equal the committed blobs on
# every OS. With core.autocrlf=true a Windows checkout rewrote public/*.html to
# CRLF, which changed the hashes and made scripts/embed_public_assets.py --check
# (and the hosted-surface contract test) fail on Windows while passing on the
# LF-based CI runner. Pin these paths to LF so the manifest is reproducible
# everywhere instead of depending on the developer's git config.
public/** text eol=lf
api/public_assets.py text eol=lf

# Generated artifacts that must stay byte-stable.
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
